steps.body:
A loop can sit inside another loop. The inner loop runs **all** of its passes for every single pass of the outer loop, so 3 outer passes of 4 inner passes run the inner body 12 times.

For a grid, name the counters `row` and `col`, build each row as a string in the inner loop, and print it once after the inner loop:

```javascript
for (let row = 1; row <= 2; row++) {
  let line = "";
  for (let col = 1; col <= 3; col++) {
    line += `${row}${col} `;
  }
  console.log(line); // "11 12 13 " then "21 22 23 "
}
```

Declare `line` inside the outer loop so every row starts empty. The inner loop can use the outer counter, either in its condition (`col <= row` makes each row longer) or in its body.

To put a space only *between* values, add it before every value except the first: `if (col > 1) { line += " "; }`.

A plain `break` in the inner loop only ends the inner loop. To leave both, label the outer loop (`outer: for (...)`) and write `break outer;`.

